.IX Title "URI::smb 3"
.TH URI::smb 3 "2025-09-17" "perl v5.34.3" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
URI::smb \- Samba/CIFS URI scheme
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    my $uri = URI\->new(\*(Aqsmb://authdomain;user:password@server/share/path\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This module implements the (unofficial) \f(CW\*(C`smb:\*(C'\fR \s-1URI\s0 scheme described in <http://www.ubiqx.org/cifs/Appendix\-D.html>.
.SH "SUBROUTINES/METHODS"
.IX Header "SUBROUTINES/METHODS"
.SS "default_port"
.IX Subsection "default_port"
The default port for accessing Samba/Windows File Servers is 445
.SS "user"
.IX Subsection "user"
Get or set the user part of the \s-1URI\s0 (without the authdomain)
.SS "authdomain"
.IX Subsection "authdomain"
Get or set the authentication authdomain part of the \s-1URI.\s0 This value is only available if the user is already set.
.SS "sharename"
.IX Subsection "sharename"
Helper method to get the share name from path
.SH "DEPENDENCIES"
.IX Header "DEPENDENCIES"
None
.SH "BUGS AND LIMITATIONS"
.IX Header "BUGS AND LIMITATIONS"
See \s-1URI\s0
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
<http://www.ubiqx.org/cifs/Appendix\-D.html>
.SH "AUTHOR"
.IX Header "AUTHOR"
I. M. Bur <github@lty.cz>
